# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend ↔ backend API base URL
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This app serves the React SPA and the Django REST API from the SAME Render
# web service (https://nwtcs.onrender.com). Leave REACT_APP_API_URL UNSET so
# that the Axios client in src/api/axios.js defaults to the same-origin
# relative path "/api/". Login then posts to
# https://nwtcs.onrender.com/api/token/ — the route registered in sacco/urls.py
# as path "api/token/" (accounts.auth_views.custom_token_obtain).
#
# Only set REACT_APP_API_URL when the frontend is hosted on a DIFFERENT origin
# than the backend (for example a SPA on Vercel talking to this Render API). In
# that case set it in the hosting platform's environment variables — NOT here —
# and never commit a placeholder such as https://your-backend.onrender.com/api/.
# A Jest guard (src/api/axios.test.js) fails the build if a placeholder host is
# committed in this file.
#
# Example (leave commented unless the SPA is hosted on a separate origin):
# REACT_APP_API_URL=https://api.nwtcs.co.ke/api/
